<p><b>Which stages are scored.</b> Every quiz stage, and every interaction stage that finishes with <code>done()</code> (expression builds, sharing, filling rows, symbol taps, step-by-step, ordering, multi-pick, the flip carousel), records "right first time or not" under the id <code>step * 10 + stage index</code> (so stage 3 of screen 12 is 123). Turn stages (Situations, Operator and Job turns) never record anything. Details in 5.1.</p>
<p><b>Flow:</b> after the last stage of a screen, Continue goes to <code>operatorsNext(step)</code>: the next screen, a screen skipped for a strong learner, or a one-time detour back to the screen that taught the idea (5.2). After screen 40 the gem popup opens ("Complete Chapter"), then <code>complete</code>. After <code>complete</code> and its reward chest, Continue returns to <code>/level</code>, where Hex moves on to the next block.</p>
<p><b>Entry:</b> on the path (<code>/level</code>) the learner taps Start on module 5. <code>onStart</code> clears every module's saved score and flow (<code>resetOperatorsScore</code>, <code>resetOperatorsFlow</code> and the others) and opens <code>/module/operators?step=1</code>. There is no resume in the middle of the module.</p>

<h3>Headlines</h3>
<p>The headline is the PDF's headline with a teal word or phrase (marked <code>*like this*</code> in the source). Its size and line count come from its length (<code>parseTitle</code>, see 4.1): up to 25 letters it stays on one line, longer ones wrap to two lines inside the 340 px column at 24 px.</p>
