<tr><td>1</td><td>Turn: operator</td><td>Next, //: floor division. It counts the complete groups.</td><td>Card 2 lit; the picture keeps the complete groups bright and fades the leftovers.</td><td>// Floor division | "Floor division: complete groups" | 23 // 4 = 5</td><td>No result panel. Nothing recorded. Continue goes to the next stage.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>Turn: operator</td><td>Last, %: modulus. It gives what is left over.</td><td>Card 3 lit; the picture fades the complete groups and keeps the leftovers bright.</td><td>% Modulus | "Modulus: the remainder" | 23 % 4 = 3</td><td>No result panel. Nothing recorded. Continue goes to the next stage.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>Quiz, rows</td><td>What does 23 // 4 = 5 tell us?</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td><span class="ok">✔ 5 complete groups of 4.</span><br>5 chocolates are left over.<br>The decimal answer, 5.75.</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": Floor division rounds the quotient down: the number of complete groups.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": // counts how many complete groups fit. It is not the leftover.</td></tr>
</table>


