</table>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Kind</th><th>Hex says</th><th>On screen</th><th>Answers, keys or blocks (✔ = right)</th><th>Result panel</th></tr>
<tr><td>0</td><td>Quiz, 2 x 2 tiles</td><td>Do both expressions give the same result?</td><td>SideBySide: "2 + 3 * 4" and "( 2 + 3 ) * 4".<br>Option pictures: icon-goal.svg and icon-short.svg.</td><td>Yes.<br><span class="ok">✔ No.</span></td><td>Right panel "No!": Same numbers, different results. Let's see how each is worked out.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Look at the parentheses. Could they change what happens first?</td></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Interaction: StepStage (6.5)</td><td>Watch how 2 + 3 * 4 is worked out.</td><td>Expression 2 + 3 * 4 (tokens 0 to 4).</td><td>Step 1: picks out 3 * 4 (tokens 2-4): "First, 3 * 4 is picked out."<br>Step 2: same tokens: "3 * 4 = 12."<br>Step 3: picks out 2 + (tokens 0-1): "Then add 2: 2 + 12." result 14</td><td>No result panel.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>Interaction: StepStage</td><td>Now (2 + 3) * 4.</td><td>Expression ( 2 + 3 ) * 4 (tokens 0 to 6).</td><td>Step 1: tokens 0-4: "First, the part inside the parentheses."<br>Step 2: tokens 1-3: "2 + 3 = 5."<br>Step 3: tokens 5-6: "Then multiply 5 by 4." result 20</td><td>Finish panel "14 and 20!": Parentheses group values. They can change what is calculated first, and so the result.</td></tr>
</table>


