<tr><th>#</th><th>Kind</th><th>Hex says</th><th>On screen</th><th>Answers, keys or blocks (✔ = right)</th><th>Result panel</th></tr>
<tr><td>0</td><td>Quiz, rows</td><td>A student has ₹200 and spends ₹75. Which expression finds what remains?</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>200 + 75<br><span class="ok">✔ 200 - 75</span><br>200 * 75</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": Spending takes money away: 200 - 75.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Does the money grow, or go away?</td></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Quiz, rows</td><td>There are 6 boxes, each with 8 pencils. Which expression finds all the pencils?</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>6 + 8<br>6 // 8<br><span class="ok">✔ 6 * 8</span></td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": Equal boxes repeat: 6 * 8.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Six equal groups of 8. Which operator repeats a group?</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>Quiz, rows</td><td>17 chocolates shared among 5 students. Whole chocolates each?</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>17 % 5<br><span class="ok">✔ 17 // 5</span><br>17 / 5</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": 17 // 5 = 3 complete chocolates each.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Which operator counts complete groups?</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>Quiz, rows</td><td>Same 17 chocolates and 5 students. How many chocolates remain?</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>17 // 5<br>17 / 5<br><span class="ok">✔ 17 % 5</span></td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": 17 % 5 = 2 remain. You chose by meaning, not just by symbol.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Which operator gives the remainder?</td></tr>
</table>


