<tr><td>0</td><td>Interaction: SymbolStage</td><td>A computer compares with symbols. Tap each one.</td><td>Header: CompareDemo of the current key's example (before any tap it shows 35 &gt; 13, True).<br>Six big keys (56 px, 28 px text), 3 columns, no heading. Explanation card before a tap: "Tap each symbol."</td><td>Key | meaning | example | read aloud | result<br>&gt; | Greater than | 35 &gt; 13 | "Thirty-five is greater than thirteen." | True<br>&lt; | Less than | 13 &lt; 35 | "Thirteen is less than thirty-five." | True<br>== | Equal to | 10 == 10 | "Ten is equal to ten." | True<br>!= | Not equal to | 10 != 5 | "Ten is not equal to five." | True<br>&gt;= | Greater than or equal to | 35 &gt;= 35 | "Thirty-five is greater than or equal to thirty-five." | True<br>&lt;= | Less than or equal to | 13 &lt;= 35 | "Thirteen is less than or equal to thirty-five." | True<br>need = 3 different keys (the stage is done after the third)</td><td>Finish panel "Comparisons!": Each symbol compares two values. The next screens explain them one by one.</td></tr>
