<h3>Screen 22: Always Read Left to Right (/module/operators?step=22)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Headline</td><td>"Always Read Left to Right" (teal: "Left to Right"), one line at 24 px</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Read a comparison from left to right: the side of the symbol touching the left number is open (greater) or closed (smaller).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Stages</td><td>3 (2 step-throughs + question)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Recorded</td><td>Stage 0 (id 220) records a right when its step-through ends; stage 1 likewise (221); stage 2 is a question (222). The first step-through has no result panel.</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Kind</th><th>Hex says</th><th>On screen</th><th>Answers, keys or blocks (✔ = right)</th><th>Result panel</th></tr>
<tr><td>0</td><td>Interaction: StepStage</td><td>First, look at the left side!</td><td>Expression 8 &gt; 5.</td><td>Step 1: token 0: "Start with the number on the left: 8."<br>Step 2: token 1: "The side of the symbol touching 8 is open."<br>Step 3: tokens 0-2: "So the left number is greater: “Eight is greater than five.”"</td><td>No result panel.</td></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Interaction: StepStage</td><td>Now a second example.</td><td>Expression 5 &lt; 8.</td><td>Step 1: token 0: "Start with the number on the left: 5."<br>Step 2: token 1: "The side of the symbol touching 5 is closed."<br>Step 3: tokens 0-2: "So the left number is smaller: “Five is less than eight.”"</td><td>Finish panel "The rule": Left side open: the left number is greater. Left side closed: the left number is smaller.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>Quiz, rows</td><td>In 6 &lt; 11 the left side is closed. What does that tell us?</td><td>ExprBig: 6 &lt; 11 at 40 px.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td><span class="ok">✔ 6 is smaller than 11.</span><br>6 is greater than 11.</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": Left side closed: the left number is smaller.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Start from the left number and look at the side touching it.</td></tr>
</table>


