<h3>Screen 25: Six Ways to Compare Values! (/module/operators?step=25)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Headline</td><td>"Six Ways to Compare Values!" (teal: "Compare Values!"), two lines at 24 px</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purpose</td><td>The six comparison operators with meaning, example and how they read; = against ==.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Stages</td><td>2 (Tap six keys + question)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Recorded</td><td>Quiz stages and finished interactions record: ids 250, 251.</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Kind</th><th>Hex says</th><th>On screen</th><th>Answers, keys or blocks (✔ = right)</th><th>Result panel</th></tr>
<tr><td>0</td><td>Interaction: SymbolStage</td><td>Tap each card: its meaning, an example and how it reads.</td><td>Six big keys, 3 columns, no header, no heading. Explanation card prompt: "Tap each symbol."</td><td>Key | meaning | example | read aloud | result<br>== | Equal to | 10 == 10 | "Ten is equal to ten." | True<br>!= | Not equal to | 10 != 5 | "Ten is not equal to five." | True<br>&gt; | Greater than | 10 &gt; 5 | "Ten is greater than five." | True<br>&lt; | Less than | 5 &lt; 10 | "Five is less than ten." | True<br>&gt;= | Greater than or equal to | 10 &gt;= 10 | "Ten is greater than or equal to ten." | True<br>&lt;= | Less than or equal to | 5 &lt;= 10 | "Five is less than or equal to ten." | True<br>need = all 6</td><td>Finish panel "Six operators!": Each symbol asks a different question about two values.</td></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Quiz, rows</td><td>In Python, = gives a value a name. Which symbol checks if two values are equal?</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>=<br><span class="ok">✔ ==</span><br>!=</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": == checks whether two values are equal. A single = is used for assignment.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": One of these asks “Is it equal?” and does not give a name.</td></tr>
</table>


