<h3>Screen 31: Choose the Right Operation (/module/operators?step=31)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Headline</td><td>"Choose the Right Operation" (teal: "Right Operation"), two lines at 24 px</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Choose the right operator for nine situations (arithmetic and comparison).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Stages</td><td>9 (9 "which operator" questions)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Scene</td><td>Every stage is a 2 x 2 tile question (option text 15 px). Option texts used: "+ Add", "- Subtract", "* Multiply", "/ Divide", "// Whole groups", "% Remainder", "&gt;= At least", "== Equal to", "&lt; Below", "&gt; Greater than", "&lt;= At most", "!= Not equal". Right title "Exactly!" on all.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Recorded</td><td>Every stage is a question: ids 310, 311, 312, 313, 314, 315, 316, 317, 318.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Adaptive path</td><td>Skipped for a strong learner when screen(s) 18 and 30 were answered clean.</td></tr>
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Kind</th><th>Hex says</th><th>On screen</th><th>Answers, keys or blocks (✔ = right)</th><th>Result panel</th></tr>
<tr><td>0</td><td>Quiz, 2 x 2 tiles</td><td>Find the total price of two products.</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td><span class="ok">✔ + Add</span><br>- Subtract<br>* Multiply<br>/ Divide</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": Adding combines the two prices.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Which operator puts two values together?</td></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Quiz, 2 x 2 tiles</td><td>Find the balance left after spending money.</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>* Multiply<br><span class="ok">✔ - Subtract</span><br>+ Add<br>/ Divide</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": Subtracting finds what remains.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Spending takes money away.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>Quiz, 2 x 2 tiles</td><td>Find the total chairs in 4 equal rows of 5.</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>+ Add<br>/ Divide<br><span class="ok">✔ * Multiply</span><br>- Subtract</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": Equal rows repeat: multiply.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Equal groups call for a shortcut.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>Quiz, 2 x 2 tiles</td><td>Share 10 litres of juice among 4 friends. Find the exact amount each.</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>// Whole groups<br><span class="ok">✔ / Divide</span><br>% Remainder<br>* Multiply</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": Ordinary division gives the exact share, 2.5.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": You want the exact amount, decimals included.</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>Quiz, 2 x 2 tiles</td><td>Share 17 chocolates among 5 students. Find the whole chocolates each.</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>/ Divide<br>% Remainder<br><span class="ok">✔ // Whole groups</span><br>- Subtract</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": Floor division gives complete groups: 3 each.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Which operator counts complete groups?</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>Quiz, 2 x 2 tiles</td><td>Find how many chocolates remain after forming complete groups.</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>// Whole groups<br><span class="ok">✔ % Remainder</span><br>/ Divide<br>+ Add</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": Modulus gives the remainder.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Which operator gives what is left over?</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>Quiz, 2 x 2 tiles</td><td>Check whether a score reaches 100.</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>&lt; Below<br><span class="ok">✔ &gt;= At least</span><br>== Equal to<br>+ Add</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": &gt;= includes 100 itself: “at least 100”.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Reaching 100 means 100 or more.</td></tr>
<tr><td>7</td><td>Quiz, 2 x 2 tiles</td><td>Check whether two values are equal.</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>&gt; Greater than<br><span class="ok">✔ == Equal to</span><br>&lt; Below<br>!= Not equal</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": == checks equality.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Which one asks “Is it the same?”</td></tr>
<tr><td>8</td><td>Quiz, 2 x 2 tiles</td><td>Check that a value is below a limit. The limit itself is not allowed.</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>&lt;= At most<br><span class="ok">✔ &lt; Below</span><br>&gt;= At least<br>== Equal to</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": &lt; leaves the limit out. &lt;= would allow it.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Is the limit itself allowed?</td></tr>
</table>


