<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Kind</th><th>Hex says</th><th>On screen</th><th>Answers, keys or blocks (✔ = right)</th><th>Result panel</th></tr>
<tr><td>0</td><td>Interaction: ExpressionStage</td><td>4 notebooks at ₹25, 3 pens at ₹10. They pay ₹150. Build the change.</td><td>Lead: ValueCards: notebook "4 notebooks" ₹25 each, pen "3 pens" ₹10 each, coins "Pays" ₹150.<br>11 places (tight sizes); result slot.</td><td>Blocks: 150, 4, 25, 3, 10, *, *, +, -, (, )<br>Right: 150 - ( the 8 ways of 4 * 25 + 3 * 10 ) with the brackets, for example 150 - ( 4 * 25 + 3 * 10 )<br>Result: 20<br>Wrong-try note: "Total the notebooks and the pens first, in parentheses. Then take it from 150."</td><td>Finish panel "₹20 back!": Notebooks 100 + pens 30 = 130. Then 150 - 130 = 20.</td></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Quiz, rows</td><td>What if the student pays only ₹120? What is 120 - 130?</td><td>ExprBig: 120 - 130 at 36 px.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>10<br><span class="ok">✔ -10</span><br>0</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": 120 - 130 = -10. The student is ₹10 short: a shortfall, not money back.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": The student pays less than the bill. Which way is the difference?</td></tr>
</table>


<h3>Screen 33: Create a Shopping Calculator (/module/operators?step=33)</h3>
