</table>
<table>
<tr><th>#</th><th>Kind</th><th>Hex says</th><th>On screen</th><th>Answers, keys or blocks (✔ = right)</th><th>Result panel</th></tr>
<tr><td>0</td><td>Interaction: OrderStage (6.6)</td><td>Put the shopping app's steps in order.</td><td>Lead: ValueCards: notebook "Notebooks", pen "Pens", gift "Pencils" (no values).</td><td>Right order: 1 Keep the price of each item. 2 Ask how many of each item. 3 Multiply price by quantity for each item. 4 Add the three totals. 5 Display the final bill.<br>Shown in this order: "Multiply price by quantity for each item.", "Display the final bill.", "Keep the price of each item.", "Add the three totals.", "Ask how many of each item."<br>Wrong-tap note: "The app needs prices and quantities before it can calculate."</td><td>Finish panel "A working plan!": Price * quantity for each item, then add the three totals.</td></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Quiz, rows</td><td>How does the app find the cost of one kind of item?</td><td>No picture.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td><span class="ok">✔ notebook_price * notebook_quantity</span><br>notebook_price + notebook_quantity<br>notebook_price - notebook_quantity</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": Multiplication calculates repeated item costs. Addition combines the different totals.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Several items, each with the same price: which operator?</td></tr>
</table>


