<tr><td>3</td><td>Quiz, rows</td><td>Each bus costs ₹2,000. Which expression finds the cost of 4 buses?</td><td>TripFacts.<br>Option pictures: neutral icons.</td><td>4 + 2000<br><span class="ok">✔ 4 * 2000</span><br>4 // 2000</td><td>Right panel "Exactly!": 4 * 2000 = 8000.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Four buses, each with the same cost.</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>Quiz, 2 x 2 tiles</td><td>The budget is ₹7,000. What does 8000 &lt;= 7000 give?</td><td>TripFacts.<br>Option pictures: icon-goal.svg and icon-short.svg.</td><td>True<br><span class="ok">✔ False</span></td><td>Right panel "False!": The school needs ₹8,000 but has ₹7,000, so the trip can't be arranged within budget.<br>Wrong panel "Not quite": Is 8000 less than or equal to 7000?</td></tr>
</table>


<h3>Screen 38: Why Did You Choose These Operations? (/module/operators?step=38)</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Headline</td><td>"Why Did You Choose These Operations?" (teal: "These Operations?"), two lines at 24 px</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Explain why each operator was chosen.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Stages</td><td>6 (6 "why" questions)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Scene</td><td>Every right panel is titled "Well explained!". The detour depends on which stages were missed (5.2).</td></tr>
