<h2>8. Lesson complete screen (/module/operators?step=complete)</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<tr><td>Component</td><td><code>LessonCompleteScreen level=5 accuracy=operatorsAccuracy</code>: the shared screen, with this module's accuracy.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Display</td><td>Full-screen Rive artboard <code>LESSON_Complete</code> (<code>LessonComplete_SM</code>, view model <code>LessonComplete</code>, from <code>hex.riv</code>), fit width, centred, held to 430 px wide on a wide screen. No header.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Values written</td><td>Once ready: <code>xp = 40</code>, <code>accuracy</code> = the share of recorded questions right the first time (5.1; 100 if none), <code>time = 222</code> seconds (a fixed value, shown as 3:42). Written as numbers, or as text ("+40", "92%", "3:42") if the artboard declares strings. Then the <code>play</code> trigger fires and the phone vibrates once for 1.2 s.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Continue</td><td>The solo Continue button (module button, full phone width). It calls <code>completeModule(5)</code>: the path's saved count of finished modules becomes 5 (only if it was lower; replaying changes nothing) and a one-time "just done" flag is set so the path plays Hex moving on. Then it shows the reward chest on the same URL.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reward chest (RewardScreen)</td><td>"REWARD_BG" (sunburst, full-screen, cover) with "REWARD_Chest" on it (440 x 430 artboard drawn 150 vw wide, max 640 px, centred at 44% of the height). A full-screen button takes taps: each tap sets the chest's <code>tap</code> to 1, 2, 3 (two wobbles, then the lid opens); a short haptic on taps 1 and 2, the long claim buzz on the third. About 1.9 s after the third tap the Continue button slides in. Continue resets the review record and goes to <code>/level</code>, where Hex moves on to the next block. See module-rive-animations section 11b.</td></tr>
</table>

